# Build context hygiene: everything the image builds from is copied explicitly in the Dockerfile,
# so this list mostly guards against a stray local artifact (a populated node_modules, a real .env,
# a data/ directory full of presets) silently ending up in a layer.
.git
.github
.gitignore
.claude
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
web/dist
data
.env
.env.*
!.env.sample
*.log
.nyc_output
coverage
*.tsbuildinfo
docs
test
scripts
docker-compose*.yaml
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
*.md
.DS_Store

# Must come last: the final matching pattern wins, and `docs` above excludes this whole subtree
# from the build context — which is not a hypothetical, it is how the Dockerfile's
# `COPY docs/wing-protocol` came to fail with `"/docs/wing-protocol": not found`.
# The wing-docs:// MCP resources read these files at runtime from the package root
# (src/plugins/wing/resources.ts), so the image genuinely needs them; the rest of docs/ it does not.
!docs/wing-protocol
!docs/wing-protocol/**
